    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="1183" n="1163" xml:id="pg1163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/11–1650</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of Defense</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-16">November 16,
                        1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Department of State
                    has learned through reliable channels that the Indian Ambassador to Peiping, Mr.
                    Pannikar, has reported that the Counselor of the Soviet Embassy in Peiping told
                    him that if United Nations planes bomb Manchuria, they would be attacked by the
                    Air Force of the Soviet Union.</p>
                <p>Although you may wish to pass this information to General MacArthur, it is
                    requested that special security precautions be used because of the extreme
                    sensitivity of the source.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
